Path('workspace/agent3_general_ear_lemma.md').write_text(r'''# General lex-ear inflation lemma (reviewed by agents 1, 2, 3)

Let K be a pure two-dimensional complex admitting a pure shelling in which every facet after the first has restriction face of size one or two. Replace each vertex v by a block B_v of m vertices, and let Y_r be the complex with facets all r-subsets of unions of three blocks corresponding to facets of K. For r>=4 and m>=r, Y_r is 1-decomposable.

Proof: induct on the number of old shelling facets. Let F be the last old triangle, with restriction sigma. All faces containing sigma occur only in F. If sigma={a}, remove clone vertices of B_a one by one. Every link is a full pure skeleton of a simplex on the remaining vertices of the expanded cluster F, hence vertex-decomposable. A ridge stranded by removing a clone can be extended using an unused clone from any old block in F minus sigma; this block has m>=r clones and the ridge has only r-1 vertices. The resulting rank-r face avoids the removed clone and all formerly removed clone vertices. Thus every deletion is pure. At the end, only the expanded previous prefix remains.

If sigma={a,b}, enumerate B_a={a_1,...,a_m}, B_b={b_1,...,b_m}, and write C for the third block. Remove the clone edges a_i b_j in lexicographic order (i,j). Before removing a_i b_j, the permissible remaining clones in its link are a_{i+1},...,a_m and b_{j+1},...,b_m, together with all of C. Every subset of these vertices of size at most r-2 is in the link: previously removed pairs lie either in an earlier row or an earlier column of row i, and none can occur in such a subset together with a_i b_j. No other old triangle contains the old pair ab. Consequently the link is exactly the full (r-3)-skeleton of the simplex on these allowed vertices, hence vertex-decomposable.

To prove purity of each deletion, take a ridge of a facet containing the current edge and remove either endpoint of that edge. Add an unused C-vertex, possible since |C|=m>=r and the ridge has r-1 vertices. This introduces no forbidden clone pair. If the ridge still meets both B_a and B_b, the extension belongs to the surviving new cluster. If one block is absent, the ridge lies in an old expanded boundary edge of F, and the extension lies in the expanded previous prefix. Thus all newly exposed faces extend to rank-r facets.

After deleting all pairs, no face meets both B_a and B_b; the remainder is exactly the expanded previous prefix. The induction ends at the uniform rank-r skeleton on three blocks, which is vertex-decomposable. Every removed face has size at most two, proving 1-decomposability.

The explicit 28-triangle K in agent3_2core_order.json has this ear shelling and has complete graph and no tetrahedron containing three or four K-triangles. Thus its inflation has a complete graph, tetrahedron-closed noncomplete triangle set, and is 1-decomposable. The core invariant in agent3_conditional_lower.md therefore forces at least r-3 new vertices to complete it. With r=d+1 this gives the stronger b(d,k)>=d-2 for every k>=1. Together with the proved upper bound it implies b(d,k)=d-2 for all d>=3, k>=1. This stronger statement has been independently finite-checked at r=4,m=4 and r=5,m=5 by agent1.
''')
print('updated conditional file; wrote full general ear proof')